1
00:00:02,450 --> 00:00:06,625
{\an8}You can add any Android app from your phone to a button on the dash.

2
00:00:10,300 --> 00:00:15,250
{\an8}The app opens in the large main area of the dash, usually where the map is.

3
00:00:16,800 --> 00:00:20,475
{\an8}To show an app full screen, put it in its own sub dash.

4
00:00:22,525 --> 00:00:25,175
{\an8}Then open that sub dash with a button.

5
00:00:26,025 --> 00:00:28,975
{\an8}These sub dashes all open full screen.

6
00:00:30,175 --> 00:00:33,725
{\an8}The main area can be resized, as big as you like.

7
00:00:34,975 --> 00:00:39,300
{\an8}For the best experience, keep full-screen apps in their own sub dash.

8
00:00:42,325 --> 00:00:46,450
{\an8}Two widgets take the main space of the dash: App and Camera.

9
00:00:47,225 --> 00:00:51,400
{\an8}App shows an Android app from your phone, right inside the dash.

10
00:00:52,050 --> 00:00:56,875
{\an8}Camera shows the camera you selected in the MOTO-HUB Dashcam module.

11
00:00:58,150 --> 00:01:00,600
{\an8}It shows one camera at a time.

12
00:01:01,500 --> 00:01:06,075
{\an8}It can be any camera the module supports, not only a bike dash cam.

13
00:01:07,200 --> 00:01:10,200
{\an8}For example, an IP camera at home.

14
00:01:12,200 --> 00:01:18,050
{\an8}Dash works on any screen that supports Android Auto, and replaces Android Auto there.

15
00:01:18,800 --> 00:01:21,400
{\an8}Have fun, and see you on Discord.
